{
  "Document": [
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 1,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Type-Safe Sharing"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "One of the biggest advantages of using Rust for both the frontend and backend is the ability to share types."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "The Shared Crate Pattern"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Instead of defining the same "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "User"
        },
        {
          "Text": " struct in both the "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "src-tauri"
        },
        {
          "Text": " and "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "src"
        },
        {
          "Text": " folders, create a separate crate (e.g., "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "my-app-types"
        },
        {
          "Text": ") that both depend on."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "CodeBlock": {
        "language": "rust",
        "code": "// in shared_types/src/lib.rs\n#[derive(serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize, Clone, Debug)]\npub struct UserProfile {\n    pub id: u64,\n    pub username: String,\n    pub email: String,\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Benefits of Shared Types"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "OrderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Single Source of Truth"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ": If you add a field to "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "UserProfile"
        },
        {
          "Text": ", both the backend and frontend will be updated."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "OrderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Compile-Time Checking"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ": If the backend changes a field from a "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "String"
        },
        {
          "Text": " to an "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "Option<String>"
        },
        {
          "Text": ", the frontend code will fail to compile until you handle the "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "None"
        },
        {
          "Text": " case."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "OrderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Reduced Boilerplate"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ": No more manual JSON parsing or guessing the shape of the data coming across the bridge."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Implementation Tip"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Make sure your shared crate uses "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "serde"
        },
        {
          "Text": " and is compatible with "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "wasm32-unknown-unknown"
        },
        {
          "Text": " so it can be compiled into the Leptos frontend."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}